Subject: [PATCH 02351/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE C (ARC
 NORTH STAR; biggest reproducible-level upside) -- E3 executable-world-model
 on sc25 to CRACK the win-mechanic the BFS solver stalled on, and REPRODUCE L1
 offline. sc25 has 5 LIVE-RECORDED levels but 0 reproduced (the live
 trajectory does NOT replay offline; the from-scratch BFS solver
 arc3_sc25_offline_solver.py works infra-wise but is 'blocked on the
 win-mechanic'). The registry has rich mechanic notes: MULTIPLE win paths
 (move player 'pluyoo' to exit; OR align 9 'clcbko' goal sprites to the 3x3
 cast grid at +1,+1), ACTION6 click to select spell + toggle 3x3 cast cells at
 (24+5c,49+5r) + fire, ACTION1-4 tank-controls move. The E3 approach (INDUCE
 the spell/cast-grid/tank-control mechanic as an executable Python world
 model, the WorldModelVerifier grounds it) is the DIFFERENT approach vs the
 stalled BFS. Same explore-verify-plan harness as exp4339 (AERA 2605.25931 +
 Agent2World 2512.22336). The codex agent IS the proposer (WRITES
 results/arc_e3/sc25/world_model.py; NO nested CodexProposer). HARD gate:
 offline_reproduced=true AND reproduced_levels>=1 (a +1, opening the path to
 the 5 live-recorded levels -> up to +5 reproducible). An honest partial (best
 verifier_accuracy + the win-mechanic gap CLASS) is PROGRESS.
 verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard
 submission; cap per-task wall-time.

